  "description": "<p>Richard Green reports:</p>\n\n<p>We have recently had a small issue with oaiprovider when the British Library tried to harvest our thesis metadata.  Using the ListRecords verb results in a set of records each wrapped as</p>\n\n<p>&lt;record xmlns=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/ &lt;<a href=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/</a>&gt;  \"&gt;<br/>\n   ...<br/>\n&lt;/record&gt;</p>\n\n<p>Instead of just</p>\n\n<p>&lt;record&gt;<br/>\n...<br/>\n&lt;/record&gt;</p>\n\n<p>This caused them some problems because one of their transforms wasn't set up to deal with this response which seems, from the OAI-PMH spec, to be non-standard.</p>\n\n<p>To fix this issue, Simon removed the following from Line 173 of FedoraOAIDriver.java :-</p>\n\n<p>out.println(\"&lt;record xmlns=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/\\\"&gt;\");</p>\n\n<p>And replaced with:-</p>\n\n<p>out.println(\"&lt;record&gt;\");  </p>",
